          <!-- 3. HOW PROXEVE WORKS -->
          <section id="how-it-works" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Architecture</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">How ProxEve Works</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              ProxEve functions as a transparent, high-throughput reverse proxy tailored specifically for AI completion and embedding APIs. When your client application sends an inference request:
            </p>

            <div class="docs-card-grid">
              <div class="docs-card">
                <div class="docs-card-icon">
                  <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <polygon points="12 2 2 7 12 12 22 7 12 2"></polygon>
                    <polyline points="2 17 12 22 22 17"></polyline>
                    <polyline points="2 12 12 17 22 12"></polyline>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="docs-card-title">1. Request Ingestion</h3>
                <p class="docs-card-desc">The request is authenticated via your ProxEve API key and mapped to your project configuration.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="docs-card">
                <div class="docs-card-icon">
                  <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"></circle>
                    <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="docs-card-title">2. Cache Query</h3>
                <p class="docs-card-desc">A canonical hash of the model parameters and prompt messages is evaluated in the cache cluster.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="docs-card">
                <div class="docs-card-icon">
                  <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path>
                    <polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="docs-card-title">3. Hit Resolution</h3>
                <p class="docs-card-desc">If a valid cached record exists, ProxEve returns it immediately with <code class="code-inline">X-ProxEve-Cache: HIT</code>.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="docs-card">
                <div class="docs-card-icon">
                  <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <path d="M5 12h14"></path>
                    <path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="docs-card-title">4. Upstream Forwarding</h3>
                <p class="docs-card-desc">On a cache miss, the request forwards directly to OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini. The response is cached and returned.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 4. AUTHENTICATION -->
          <section id="authentication" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Integration</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Authentication</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              All requests to the ProxEve gateway require an authentication bearer token passed in the HTTP <code class="code-inline">Authorization</code> header:
            </p>

            <div class="macos-code-window">
              <div class="macos-window-header">
                <div class="macos-dots" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="macos-dot macos-dot-red"></span>
                  <span class="macos-dot macos-dot-yellow"></span>
                  <span class="macos-dot macos-dot-green"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="macos-window-title">http header</div>
                <button type="button" class="macos-copy-btn" data-copy-id="snippet-auth-header">
                  <span>Copy</span>
                </button>
              </div>
              <div class="macos-window-body">
                <pre id="snippet-auth-header"><code><span class="code-token-cmd">Authorization</span>: Bearer pk_live_9b4e72a8c1f0d3e5</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="docs-callout callout-info">
              <div class="docs-callout-title">Key Prefixes</div>
              ProxEve keys use standard environment prefixes: <code class="code-inline">pk_live_</code> for production traffic and <code class="code-inline">pk_test_</code> for sandbox development.
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 5. API REFERENCE -->
          <section id="api-reference" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Integration</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">API Reference</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              ProxEve is designed as a drop-in proxy compatible with the OpenAI API specification.
            </p>

            <div class="docs-table-wrapper">
              <table class="docs-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Method</th>
                    <th>Endpoint</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="badge-http-post">POST</span></td>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">/v1/chat/completions</code></td>
                    <td>Creates a model response for conversation messages with automatic caching.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="badge-http-post">POST</span></td>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">/v1/embeddings</code></td>
                    <td>Generates text vector embeddings with exact string caching.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="badge-http-get">GET</span></td>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">/v1/models</code></td>
                    <td>Lists supported upstream models routed through your active provider connections.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 6. CONFIGURATION -->
          <section id="configuration" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Integration</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Configuration</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Each project can configure caching parameters through the dashboard or HTTP control headers:
            </p>

            <ul style="padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.875rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 1rem;">
              <li><strong>TTL (Time-To-Live):</strong> Specify cache duration from 60 seconds to 30 days. Default is 24 hours.</li>
              <li><strong>Model Scoping:</strong> Cache entries are strictly partitioned by model name (e.g. <code class="code-inline">gpt-4o</code> vs <code class="code-inline">claude-3-5-sonnet</code>).</li>
              <li><strong>Temperature Handling:</strong> When temperature is 0.0, responses are cached aggressively. Queries with high temperature can be configured to bypass caching.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <!-- 7. PROVIDERS -->
          <section id="providers" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Integration</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Providers</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              ProxEve acts as a multi-model gateway supporting major AI foundation providers:
            </p>

            <div class="docs-card-grid">
              <div class="docs-card">
                <h3 class="docs-card-title">OpenAI</h3>
                <p class="docs-card-desc">Supported models include GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini, and text-embedding-3-small.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="docs-card">
                <h3 class="docs-card-title">Google Gemini</h3>
                <p class="docs-card-desc">Supported models include Gemini 1.5 Flash, Gemini 1.5 Pro, and Gemini Flash Thinking.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="docs-card">
                <h3 class="docs-card-title">Anthropic</h3>
                <p class="docs-card-desc">Supported models include Claude 3.5 Sonnet and Claude 3 Haiku.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 8. EXACT CACHING -->
          <section id="exact-caching" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Caching</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Exact Caching</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Exact caching performs deterministic normalization and cryptographic hashing of the request body. When an incoming request matches a previous prompt payload exactly, ProxEve serves the cached result with zero upstream latency.
            </p>

            <div class="docs-callout callout-info">
              <div class="docs-callout-title">Response Headers</div>
              Inspect response headers to verify cache status:
              <br />
              <code class="code-inline">X-ProxEve-Cache: HIT</code> or <code class="code-inline">X-ProxEve-Cache: MISS</code>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 9. SEMANTIC CACHING -->
          <section id="semantic-caching" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Caching</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Semantic Caching</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Semantic caching compares prompt embeddings to identify queries with identical intent even when phrasing differs (e.g., <em>"What is the capital of France?"</em> vs <em>"Tell me France's capital city"</em>).
            </p>

            <p class="docs-p">
              You can configure a semantic similarity threshold (e.g. 0.95) to balance between aggressive cache hits and response variation.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 10. CACHE CONTROLS -->
          <section id="cache-controls" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Caching</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Cache Controls</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Fine-tune caching behavior per request using custom HTTP headers:
            </p>

            <div class="docs-table-wrapper">
              <table class="docs-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Header</th>
                    <th>Value</th>
                    <th>Behavior</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">X-ProxEve-Bypass-Cache</code></td>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">true</code></td>
                    <td>Skips cache lookup and does not store the response.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">X-ProxEve-Force-Refresh</code></td>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">true</code></td>
                    <td>Executes upstream call and updates existing cache record.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">X-ProxEve-TTL</code></td>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">3600</code></td>
                    <td>Sets a custom time-to-live in seconds for this request.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 11. USAGE & METRICS -->
          <section id="usage-metrics" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Monitoring</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Usage & Metrics</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Track your application performance via the <a href="/usage" style="color:#2563eb;text-decoration:underline;">Usage Dashboard</a>. ProxEve logs real-time throughput metrics:
            </p>

            <ul style="padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.875rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 1rem;">
              <li><strong>Total Request Volume:</strong> Aggregated calls made through your gateway.</li>
              <li><strong>Cache Hit Ratio:</strong> Percentage of requests served directly from cache.</li>
              <li><strong>Latency Saved:</strong> Average roundtrip time saved per cached response.</li>
              <li><strong>Estimated Cost Avoidance:</strong> Dollar savings based on avoided upstream token charges.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <!-- 12. REQUEST LOGS -->
          <section id="request-logs" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Monitoring</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Request Logs</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              The dashboard displays an audit trail of recent requests, including HTTP status codes, cache disposition (HIT/MISS), execution latency, and token consumption for rapid debugging.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 13. ERRORS -->
          <section id="errors" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Monitoring</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Errors</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Standard HTTP error responses are returned when requests cannot be processed:
            </p>

            <div class="docs-table-wrapper">
              <table class="docs-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Code</th>
                    <th>Status</th>
                    <th>Reason & Remediation</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">401</code></td>
                    <td>Unauthorized</td>
                    <td>Missing or invalid ProxEve API key in Authorization header.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">429</code></td>
                    <td>Rate Limit Exceeded</td>
                    <td>Project throughput limit reached. Upgrade tier or throttle client.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="code-inline">502</code></td>
                    <td>Bad Gateway</td>
                    <td>Upstream AI provider encountered an error or network timeout.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 14. PROJECTS -->
          <section id="projects" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Account</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Projects</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Projects allow you to isolate caching data, API keys, and rate limits across distinct applications or deployment environments (e.g. Staging vs Production). Create and manage projects in the <a href="/project" style="color:#2563eb;text-decoration:underline;">Projects section</a>.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 15. API KEYS -->
          <section id="api-keys" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Account</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">API Keys</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Manage your credentials safely. ProxEve supports key rotation without service interruption, project-level scoping, and instant revocation from the <a href="/api-key" style="color:#2563eb;text-decoration:underline;">API Keys manager</a>.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 16. SETTINGS -->
          <section id="settings" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Account</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Settings</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              Configure global account properties, notification webhooks for low cache hit rates, security preferences, and team collaborator permissions in <a href="/setting" style="color:#2563eb;text-decoration:underline;">Settings</a>.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 17. FAQ -->
          <section id="faq" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Support</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
              <p class="docs-lead">Click on any question below to expand the answer with a smooth accordion animation.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 1 (Closed by default) -->
            <div class="docs-faq-item">
              <button type="button" class="docs-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>Does ProxEve store my prompts permanently?</span>
                <svg class="docs-faq-chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
                </svg>
              </button>
              <div class="docs-faq-answer">
                No. Cached records are ephemeral and automatically expire according to your project's configured TTL. Data is encrypted in transit and at rest.
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 2 (Closed by default) -->
            <div class="docs-faq-item">
              <button type="button" class="docs-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>What latency overhead does ProxEve add?</span>
                <svg class="docs-faq-chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
                </svg>
              </button>
              <div class="docs-faq-answer">
                ProxEve edge proxies add negligible latency (&lt; 8ms for cache misses). On cache hits, responses return in under 15ms, eliminating typical 800ms-3500ms upstream LLM execution delays.
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 3 (Closed by default) -->
            <div class="docs-faq-item">
              <button type="button" class="docs-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>Can I use ProxEve with official SDKs (Python / Node.js)?</span>
                <svg class="docs-faq-chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
                </svg>
              </button>
              <div class="docs-faq-answer">
                Yes. You only need to configure the <code class="code-inline">base_url</code> parameter in the official OpenAI Python or TypeScript SDK to point to ProxEve gateway URL.
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 4 (Closed by default) -->
            <div class="docs-faq-item">
              <button type="button" class="docs-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>How does ProxEve handle non-deterministic parameters like temperature?</span>
                <svg class="docs-faq-chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
                </svg>
              </button>
              <div class="docs-faq-answer">
                When temperature is 0, responses are completely deterministic and safely cached. When temperature is greater than 0, you can choose in your project configuration whether to cache or bypass.
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 18. TROUBLESHOOTING -->
          <section id="troubleshooting" class="docs-section">
            <div class="docs-section-header">
              <span class="docs-section-tag">Support</span>
              <h2 class="docs-h1">Troubleshooting</h2>
            </div>

            <p class="docs-p">
              If you encounter unexpected cache misses or connection issues:
            </p>

            <ul style="padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.875rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 1rem;">
              <li><strong>Verify Temperature:</strong> Non-zero temperature values may introduce slight variability if strict exact caching is required.</li>
              <li><strong>Check Header Case:</strong> Ensure your authorization header format is strictly <code class="code-inline">Authorization: Bearer &lt;key&gt;</code>.</li>
              <li><strong>Inspect Response Headers:</strong> Examine <code class="code-inline">X-ProxEve-Cache</code> in the response to diagnose whether a miss occurred due to a custom bypass header.</li>
            </ul>

            <footer class="docs-footer">
              <div>&copy; 2026 ProxEve Technologies Inc. Prototype Documentation.</div>
              <div>Need assistance? Return to the <a href="/dashboard">Dashboard Overview</a>.</div>
            </footer>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>

